# AI SDK - Structured Data Generation

`generateObject` is DEPRECATED. Use `generateText` with `Output.object()` instead.

## Output types

### `Output.object()` — structured object from a Zod schema

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER
import { generateObject } from 'ai'
const { object } = await generateObject({
    model: anthropic('claude-sonnet-4-6'),
    schema: mySchema,
    prompt: '...',
})

// ✅ ALWAYS
import { generateText, Output } from 'ai'
import { z } from 'zod'

const { output } = await generateText({
    model: anthropic('claude-sonnet-4-6'),
    output: Output.object({ schema: z.object({ name: z.string() }) }),
    prompt: '...',
})
if (!output) throw new Error('Failed to generate object')
```

### `Output.array()` — array of typed objects

```typescript
import { generateText, Output } from 'ai'
import { z } from 'zod'

const { output } = await generateText({
    model: anthropic('claude-sonnet-4-6'),
    output: Output.array({
        element: z.object({ location: z.string(), temperature: z.number() }),
    }),
    prompt: '...',
})
```

When streaming, use `elementStream` to receive each completed element:

```typescript
import { streamText, Output } from 'ai'

const { elementStream } = streamText({
    model: anthropic('claude-sonnet-4-6'),
    output: Output.array({ element: z.object({ name: z.string() }) }),
    prompt: '...',
})

for await (const element of elementStream) {
    console.log(element)
}
```

### `Output.choice()` — classification / fixed enum

```typescript
import { generateText, Output } from 'ai'

const { output } = await generateText({
    model: anthropic('claude-sonnet-4-6'),
    output: Output.choice({ options: ['positive', 'negative', 'neutral'] }),
    prompt: 'Classify the sentiment of this text: ...',
})
// output is one of the options, validated
```

### `Output.json()` — unstructured JSON (no schema validation)

```typescript
import { generateText, Output } from 'ai'

const { output } = await generateText({
    model: anthropic('claude-sonnet-4-6'),
    output: Output.json(),
    prompt: '...',
})
```

### `Output.text()` — plain text (default)

```typescript
import { generateText, Output } from 'ai'

const { output } = await generateText({
    model: anthropic('claude-sonnet-4-6'),
    output: Output.text(),
    prompt: '...',
})
```

## Property descriptions

Use `.describe()` on Zod fields to guide the model:

```typescript
z.object({
    name: z.string().describe('The full name of the person'),
    age: z.number().describe('Age in years'),
})
```

## Output name & description

```typescript
Output.object({
    name: 'Recipe',
    description: 'A recipe for a dish.',
    schema: z.object({ ... }),
})
```

## Error handling

```typescript
import { generateText, Output, NoObjectGeneratedError } from 'ai'

try {
    await generateText({ model, output: Output.object({ schema }), prompt })
} catch (error) {
    if (NoObjectGeneratedError.isInstance(error)) {
        console.log('Cause:', error.cause)
        console.log('Text:', error.text)
        console.log('Response:', error.response)
        console.log('Usage:', error.usage)
    }
}
```

## Combining with tools

```typescript
import { generateText, Output, tool, stepCountIs } from 'ai'

const { output } = await generateText({
    model: anthropic('claude-sonnet-4-6'),
    tools: { myTool: tool({ ... }) },
    output: Output.object({ schema }),
    stopWhen: stepCountIs(5), // structured output counts as a step
    prompt: '...',
})
```
